build
build-*
*.dSYM
tmp.hpp
tmp.txt
.no_git
chesso_engine.log
config.json
.ref-builds

# The corpus, the fit outputs and the logs stay out: selfplay_v2.tsv alone is
# 715 MB and every one of them is reproducible from a recorded command. The
# scripts do not -- anchors.py is the only executable record of how the pinned
# test values are derived, including the quiescence composite no evaluation
# model can produce. Children of an ignored directory cannot be re-included,
# hence the star.
.tuning/*
!.tuning/*.py
.reprofile

.claude/settings.local.json

# S104. The PGO profile and its instrumented build directory. Regenerated per
# build by build_release.sh and never committed: a profile is a property of one
# workload run against one source tree, and a stale one reads as provenance.
# build-release-<arch>/ is already covered by the build-* above.
.pgo

# S105. The unbalanced SPRT book. UHO_Lichess_4852_v1.epd is 175 MB and is
# reproducible from a URL and two pinned digests, so books/fetch_book.sh
# fetches it rather than the history carrying it -- the same trade .tuning/
# makes. books/8moves_v3.pgn stays committed: it is 8.0 MB and rating.sh
# still plays it.
books/UHO_*
books/*.zip

# S084. SPSA run directories: the frozen config, the checkpoint, the trajectory,
# the engine snapshot and the run's PGN. Same trade as .ref-builds/ and
# .tuning/ -- reproducible from a committed config and a seed, and the engine
# snapshot alone is 5 MB per run. A trajectory that decides anything is copied
# into adocs/data/ by the step that reads it.
.spsa

# Python bytecode from the tools/ modules, which the tests import directly.
__pycache__
